Technical -5%, Behavioral +10%, Leadership +20%. Description and category adjustments both update per scenario.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-10\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Category-level adjustment: dragged Leadership \\\"Level Change\\\" from -2 to 0 and the panel display updated correctly. Run Simulation applied Technical -1 / Behavioral +10% / Leadership -10% / Domain -1: coverage 79%→71%, avg level 3.8→3.3, critical path 4, risk gaps 0→1 with alert naming Market Knowledge — matches hand-computed 335/475=70.5%→71% and 20/6=3.3. Reset restored coverage 79%, avg 3.8, critical path 4, gaps 0.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-11\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Save does not persist edits; reopening the model discards all level/weight/enabled changes\", \"actual\": \"Edited Sales Manager until coverage 54% / avg 2.3 / 3 risk gaps, clicked Save (no confirmation toast shown), navigated Back to the model list and reopened Sales Manager: metrics returned to the pristine coverage 79% / avg 3.8 / critical path 4 / gaps 0. Nothing is written anywhere — localStorage, sessionStorage, cookies are all empty and indexedDB.databases() returns [] both before and after Save — so a page reload cannot restore anything either.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-12\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Direct edits are bounded by construction: only set-level-1..5 buttons exist, and the weight slider exposes aria-valuemin=\\\"10\\\" / aria-valuemax=\\\"100\\\". Simulations clamp correctly: 10 cumulative Training runs (+1 level) capped levels at 5; 60 cumulative Recruitment runs (level -1/-2, weight ±10%) drove values to the floors without breaching them — observed min level 1, max level 5, min weight 0.10, max weight 1.00 across all 70 sampled states; zero out-of-range values detected.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"No reload in any case. Level: Negotiation → level 1 changed coverage 79%→63% and the progress indicator to translateX(-37.234%) (=62.8%), avg 3.8→3.2. Weight: dragging Negotiation weight slider changed coverage 79%→77%. Enabled-state: disabling CRM changed coverage 79%→81%, avg 3.8→4.0. All updated instantly.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-19\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Initially selected Recruitment scenario is not initialized — its default adjustments are missing and running it has no effect\", \"actual\": \"On first load of the detail editor the Recruitment tab is active but every category shows \\\"Level Change 0 / Weight Change 0%\\\". Clicking Run Simulation without switching tabs left all outputs unchanged (coverage 79%, avg 3.8, critical path 4, gaps 0). Only after visiting Training/Promotion and returning to Recruitment do its real defaults appear: Technical -1, Behavioral +10%, Leadership -2 / -10%, Domain -1 — proving defaults exist but were never loaded for the initial tab.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-20\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Graph controls never re-render with the current value/state after an edit, so indicators disagree with the summary and subsequent edits start from a stale state\", \"actual\": \"Weight edit: dragging negotiation weight slider changed coverage 79%→77% (model weight ~55%) while the control still showed \\\"95%\\\", aria-valuenow=95 and thumb left:calc(94.4444% - 8.88889px). Enabled-state edit: disabling CRM changed coverage to 81%/avg 4.0 while the node kept its \\\"Critical\\\" badge and border-node-critical class and the switch stayed aria-checked=\\\"true\\\"; graph highlighting therefore disagrees with the summary (summary excluded it from coverage, graph still shows it as an active Critical node). Subsequent edits start from the stale state: a 2nd click on the toggle re-issued \\\"disable\\\" instead of re-enabling (coverage stayed 81%).\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"React Flow graph: nodes show competency name + description + category + Level + Weight; 5 edges use arrowclosed markerEnd (directed) with visible weight labels 85%/70%/80%/60%/70%; controls provide zoom in, zoom out, fit view, toggle interactivity, plus a minimap; nodes are draggable (verified in FT-3).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-16\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Graph highlighting does not recalculate and disagrees with the critical-path summary\", \"actual\": \"After disabling Negotiation and lowering its level to 2, the summary critical path correctly recalculated to \\\"Customer Relationships, Pipeline Management, CRM Proficiency, +1\\\" (Negotiation excluded), but the graph still rendered the Negotiation node with class border-node-critical, its \\\"Critical\\\" badge, and stale \\\"Level Expert / Weight 95%\\\". No graph node highlighting changed at all (node classes identical to the pre-edit baseline). Summary and graph therefore contradict each other.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Negotiation (weight 95%, recommended 5) set to level 1 → gaps 0→1 immediately, alert text \\\"1 competency below recommended level: Negotiation...\\\". Restoring level 5 → gaps back to 0, alert removed. Re-lowering to level 2 → gap returns; then disabling Negotiation → gaps 0 and alert removed (coverage 74%).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"With 1 gap, metrics.gap-alert renders inside the model.metrics region directly under the four metric cards: role=\\\"alert\\\", warning styling (border-warning/50 bg-warning/5), lucide-triangle-alert icon, heading \\\"Competency Gap Alert\\\" and body \\\"1 competency below recommended level: Negotiation. Consider increasing training focus or adjusting expectations.\\\" — names the competency and suggests corrective action.\"}]}"
