    "role": "assistant",
    "type": "assistant_message",
    "content": "All 19 checklist items have been tested and recorded — coverage is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\n**11 PASS / 8 FAIL**\n\n**Passing:** search & filtering (FT-1), model detail navigation (FT-2), node dragging (FT-3), template library browsing (FT-6), scenario switching (FT-9), scenario simulation & reset (FT-10), value clamping (CS-12), live coverage updates (IX-13), graph rendering & pan/zoom (CT-15), risk-gap detection lifecycle (CT-17), gap alert presentation (CT-18).\n\n**Key defects found:**\n\n1. **Stale graph rendering (root cause of 4 failures — FT-5, FT-7, IX-20, CT-16).** The React Flow graph component never re-renders after state changes. The analysis panel updates correctly, but node level/weight text, toggle states, \"Critical\" badges, and even the entire competency set stay frozen at their initial values. Applying the Data Scientist template correctly changed the title, metrics and scenario categories, yet the graph still displayed all six Sales Manager competencies.\n\n2. **Competencies cannot be re-enabled (FT-5).** Because the switch keeps `aria-checked=\"true\"`, a second click re-issues \"disable\" instead of enabling. Disabled competencies are permanently stuck until Reset.\n\n3. **No relationship-weight editing (FT-4).** Edge weights are static labels; clicking or double-clicking an edge only selects it — no editor, dialog, or input exists.\n\n4. **No persistence whatsoever (FT-8, FT-11).** \"Save\" and \"Save Current\" are both no-ops: nothing is written to localStorage, sessionStorage, cookies, or IndexedDB. There is no \"My Templates\" collection anywhere in the app, and reopening an edited model discards all changes.\n\n5. **Uninitialized default scenario (IX-19).** The Recruitment tab is active on load but shows all-zero adjustments; running it does nothing. Its real defaults (Technical −1, Leadership −2/−10%, etc.) only appear after switching to another tab and back."
  }
}
